---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { fanPaths, resolvePath, SERIES_LABEL } from '../lib/fan';
import { allEpisodes } from '../lib/data';
const eps = await allEpisodes();
const counts = Object.fromEntries(Object.keys(SERIES_LABEL).map((s) => [s, eps.filter((e) => e.data.series === s).length]));
const first = fanPaths().find((p) => p.slug === 'first-ten')!;
const firstSteps = await resolvePath(first);
const others = await Promise.all(fanPaths().filter((p) => p.slug !== 'first-ten').map(async (p) => ({ p, n: (await resolvePath(p)).length })));
---
<Base title="Start here" description="New to The Twilight Zone? What the show is, which series to start with, the first ten episodes to watch, and how to use this site.">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="kicker">New to the Zone?</p>
    <h1>Start here</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The Twilight Zone is an anthology: every episode is a self-contained story with new characters, so you can
      start anywhere. Rod Serling created it for CBS in 1959, wrote most of the first series and introduced every
      episode on camera. It has been revived three times since, and its ideas turn up in films, songs, books and
      everyday speech.
    </p>
  </section>

  <h2>The four television series</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    {Object.entries(SERIES_LABEL).map(([s, label]) => (
      <a class="card" href={`/series/${s}/`}>
        <span class="count">{counts[s]}</span>
        <h3>{label}</h3>
        <p>{{
          '1959': 'Black and white, mostly half an hour, five seasons on CBS. Where everyone should begin.',
          '1985': 'The CBS revival, in colour, with stories by Harlan Ellison, Stephen King, Ray Bradbury and others.',
          '2002': 'A single season on UPN hosted by Forest Whitaker, including sequels and remakes of classics.',
          '2019': "Jordan Peele's two seasons for CBS All Access, which he hosts in Serling's place.",
        }[s]}</p>
      </a>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">There is also Rod Serling's second anthology, <a href="/night-gallery/">Night Gallery</a> (1970 to 1973), a 1983 <a href="/movies/">feature film</a>, radio dramas and podcasts.</p>

  <h2>Your first ten episodes</h2>
  <p>{first.short} <a href={`/paths/${first.slug}/`}>See the full path with notes</a> · <span class="path-progress small" data-progress={firstSteps.map((s) => `episodes/${s.e.id}`).join(' ')}></span></p>
  <ol class="path-steps compact">
    {firstSteps.map((s) => (
      <li data-mark={`episodes/${s.e.id}`}><a class="step-title" href={`/episodes/${s.e.id}/`}>{s.e.data.title}</a> <span class="muted small">({s.e.data.air_date?.slice(0, 4)})</span><span class="seen-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span><br /><span class="small">{s.note}</span></li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <h2>Then pick a path</h2>
  <ul class="plain">
    {others.map(({ p, n }) => <li><a href={`/paths/${p.slug}/`}><strong>{p.title}</strong></a> <span class="muted small">({n} episodes)</span><br /><span class="small">{p.short}</span></li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>Ways to explore</h2>
  <div class="grid">
    <a class="card" href="/finder/"><h3>Episode finder</h3><p>Filter every episode by series, season, decade, writer, director, actor and theme at once.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/today/"><h3>Episode of the day</h3><p>A different episode every day, plus everything that first aired on today's date.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/my-zone/"><h3>My Zone</h3><p>Your watched, owned and wanted checklist, kept in this browser with no account.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/map/"><h3>Map</h3><p>Filming locations, backlots, Serling's places, attractions and museums.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/timeline/"><h3>Timeline</h3><p>The franchise year by year, from 1959 to today.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/degrees/"><h3>Six degrees</h3><p>How any two people in the Zone are connected through the episodes they made.</p></a>
  </div>

  <h2>Where to watch</h2>
  <p>
    Every episode page links to JustWatch and Reelgood, which list current streaming, free-with-ads, rental and
    purchase options in your country. The original series has also been released on DVD and Blu-ray many times;
    each <a href="/series/1959/#releases">series page</a> lists its home-media releases.
  </p>

  <h2>About spoilers</h2>
  <p>
    Episode synopses here set up the story without giving away the ending. Where an ending is described, it is hidden
    behind a <strong>Reveal how it ends</strong> button. You can show every ending site-wide with the spoiler switch,
    and the site remembers your choice.
  </p>
</Base>
